1
00:03:45,957 --> 00:03:47,707
Oh!

2
00:03:55,999 --> 00:03:57,874
Ah!

3
00:03:59,332 --> 00:04:00,749
Doug?

4
00:04:03,082 --> 00:04:05,291
Honey, are you all right?

5
00:04:07,582 --> 00:04:10,332
You were dreaming. Doug?

6
00:04:11,416 --> 00:04:13,374
Was it about Mars?

7
00:04:19,082 --> 00:04:21,249
- Is that better?
- Hmm.

8
00:04:23,582 --> 00:04:25,249
My poor baby.

9
00:04:26,374 --> 00:04:28,749
This is getting to be an obsession.

10
00:04:36,666 --> 00:04:37,999
Was she there?

11
00:04:40,249 --> 00:04:42,082
Who?

12
00:04:43,749 --> 00:04:46,332
The one you told me about.
The brunette.

13
00:04:47,249 --> 00:04:48,791
Oh, Lori.

14
00:04:51,832 --> 00:04:54,707
I can't believe
you're jealous of a dream.

15
00:04:55,582 --> 00:04:58,249
- Who is she?
- Nobody.

16
00:04:58,457 --> 00:05:00,666
"Nobody"? What's her name?

17
00:05:00,874 --> 00:05:03,332
I don't know.

18
00:05:03,541 --> 00:05:05,374
- Tell me!
- I don't know!

19
00:05:05,582 --> 00:05:07,541
You better tell me!

20
00:05:07,749 --> 00:05:11,374
It's not funny, Doug.
You dream about her every night.

21
00:05:11,582 --> 00:05:14,124
And I'm always back in the morning.

22
00:05:14,332 --> 00:05:16,332
Let me go!

23
00:05:18,332 --> 00:05:20,416
Come on, baby.

24
00:05:20,624 --> 00:05:23,499
You know you're the girl of my dreams.

25
00:05:23,874 --> 00:05:25,457
You mean it?

26
00:05:26,582 --> 00:05:28,457
You know I do.

27
00:05:37,916 --> 00:05:40,874
I'll give you something to dream about.

28
00:05:50,666 --> 00:05:54,249
"The chairman defended the attack,
saying that space-based weapons"

29
00:05:54,457 --> 00:05:58,416
"are our only defense against the
southern block's numerical superiority."

30
00:05:58,624 --> 00:06:00,916
"And more violence last night on Mars"

31
00:06:01,124 --> 00:06:03,332
"where terrorists demanding independence"

32
00:06:03,541 --> 00:06:06,874
"once again halted the extraction
of terbinium ore."

33
00:06:11,957 --> 00:06:14,007
"Kuato and his so-called freedom brigade"

34
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:16,248
"claimed credit for this latest bombing,"

35
00:06:16,332 --> 00:06:19,916
"which attempted to reopen
the sealed-off Pyramid Mines."

36
00:06:23,207 --> 00:06:26,291
"Mars military restored order
with minimal use of force"

37
00:06:26,499 --> 00:06:30,332
"and all damage to the strategic facility
was repaired within hours."

38
00:06:30,541 --> 00:06:31,791
<i>'No cameras?</i>

39
00:06:31,999 --> 00:06:35,916
"With one mine already closed,
Mars administrator Vilos Cohaagen"

40
00:06:36,124 --> 00:06:38,332
"vowed that troops
would be used if necessary"

41
00:06:38,416 --> 00:06:41,082
"to keep production at full capacity..."

42
00:06:42,291 --> 00:06:45,999
No wonder you're having nightmares.
You're always watching the news.

43
00:06:50,082 --> 00:06:51,957
- Lori.
- Doug?

44
00:06:52,166 --> 00:06:55,582
- Let's do it.
- Do what?

45
00:06:55,791 --> 00:06:57,082
Move to Mars.

46
00:06:58,291 --> 00:07:01,582
Honey, why do you have to spoil
a perfectly wonderful morning?

47
00:07:03,332 --> 00:07:04,707
Just think about it.

48
00:07:06,916 --> 00:07:10,540
Sweetheart, we've been through this
a million times. You'd hate it on Mars.

49
00:07:10,624 --> 00:07:13,332
It's dry, it's ugly, it's boring.

50
00:07:14,666 --> 00:07:18,374
I mean, really, a revolution could
break out there any second.

51
00:07:18,582 --> 00:07:21,582
Cohaagen says it's just a few extremists.

52
00:07:21,791 --> 00:07:23,207
You believe him?

53
00:07:29,249 --> 00:07:31,541
OK. Forget about it.

54
00:07:34,457 --> 00:07:38,874
"Absolutely not. Mars was colonized by
the northern block at enormous expense."

55
00:07:39,082 --> 00:07:42,541
"Our entire war effort
depends on their terbinium."

56
00:07:42,749 --> 00:07:44,707
"It's ridiculous to think
we'd give it away"

57
00:07:44,791 --> 00:07:46,248
"just because some lazy mutants..."

58
00:07:46,332 --> 00:07:47,291
Doug.

59
00:07:49,124 --> 00:07:52,791
- Maybe we should take a trip.
- Lori, move, please.

60
00:07:52,999 --> 00:07:56,541
"...you've closed the Pyramid Mine
because you found alien artifacts?"

61
00:07:56,749 --> 00:07:59,916
There's a lot better places than Mars.

62
00:08:00,124 --> 00:08:02,957
What about Saturn?
Don't you wanna see Saturn?

63
00:08:03,166 --> 00:08:05,040
"I wish we could find some artifacts."

64
00:08:05,124 --> 00:08:07,174
"Our tourist industry could use a boost."

65
00:08:07,332 --> 00:08:09,707
Everybody says that its gorgeous.

66
00:08:09,916 --> 00:08:13,499
"Fact is, it's Mr. Kuato and his
terrorists who spread these rumors"

67
00:08:13,707 --> 00:08:15,666
"to undermine trust in the government."

68
00:08:15,874 --> 00:08:19,457
We could take a long space cruise,
the kind with nothing to do.

69
00:08:19,666 --> 00:08:23,216
- "Have you found Kuato yet?"
- "We don't even know what he looks like."

70
00:08:23,332 --> 00:08:27,291
- What do you say?
- I'm late, Lori.

71
00:08:32,499 --> 00:08:34,874
Sweetheart. Doug.

72
00:08:37,499 --> 00:08:41,582
I know it's hard being in a new town,
but let's give it a chance, OK?

73
00:08:43,624 --> 00:08:45,541
Lori, don't you understand?

74
00:08:45,749 --> 00:08:48,541
I feel like I was meant
for something more than this.

75
00:08:49,541 --> 00:08:53,332
I want to do something with my life.
I want to be somebody.

76
00:08:53,541 --> 00:08:55,457
You are somebody.

77
00:08:55,666 --> 00:08:57,582
You're the man I love.

78
00:09:02,332 --> 00:09:03,832
Bye.

79
00:09:06,291 --> 00:09:08,291
Have a nice day.

80
00:09:27,041 --> 00:09:29,999
"You are now entering a safety zone."

81
00:09:30,207 --> 00:09:34,332
"No unauthorized weapons allowed
beyond this point."

82
00:09:34,832 --> 00:09:37,832
"You are now entering a safety zone."

83
00:09:38,041 --> 00:09:42,124
"No unauthorized weapons allowed
beyond this point."

84
00:09:44,916 --> 00:09:50,249
"Would you like to ski
but you're snowed under with work?"

85
00:09:50,457 --> 00:09:54,541
"Do you dream of a vacation
at the bottom of the ocean,"

86
00:09:54,749 --> 00:09:57,041
"but you can't float the bill?"

87
00:09:57,249 --> 00:10:00,916
"Have you always wanted
to climb the mountains of Mars,"

88
00:10:02,457 --> 00:10:04,832
"but now you're over the hill?"

89
00:10:05,666 --> 00:10:07,624
"Then come to Rekall Incorporated"

90
00:10:07,832 --> 00:10:10,624
"where you can buy the memory
of your ideal vacation"

91
00:10:10,832 --> 00:10:13,374
"cheaper, safer and better
than the real thing."

92
00:10:14,124 --> 00:10:16,291
"So don't let life pass you by."

93
00:10:16,499 --> 00:10:19,832
"Call Rekall
for the memory of a life time."

94
00:10:20,041 --> 00:10:23,832
♪ 'For the memory of a lifetime

95
00:10:24,041 --> 00:10:27,541
"♪ 'Rekall, Rekall, Rekall"

96
00:10:46,166 --> 00:10:47,207
Harry.

97
00:10:49,499 --> 00:10:52,916
- Harry! You ever hear of Rekall?
- Rekall?

98
00:10:53,124 --> 00:10:54,957
Where they sell those fake memories.

99
00:10:55,166 --> 00:10:59,166
- Oh, Rekall!
- Rekall, recall, recall!

100
00:10:59,374 --> 00:11:01,582
- Thinking of going there?
- I don't know. Maybe.

101
00:11:01,666 --> 00:11:03,332
- Well, don't.
- Why not?

102
00:11:03,541 --> 00:11:05,915
A friend of mine tried
one of their special offers,

103
00:11:05,999 --> 00:11:08,457
nearly got himself Lobotomized.

104
00:11:08,791 --> 00:11:09,874
No shit?

105
00:11:10,082 --> 00:11:12,707
Don't fuck with your brain, pal.
It ain't worth it.

106
00:11:14,541 --> 00:11:16,499
I guess not.

107
00:11:58,041 --> 00:11:59,916
Hello.

108
00:12:00,791 --> 00:12:03,124
Good afternoon.
Welcome to Rekall.

109
00:12:03,332 --> 00:12:05,291
Douglas Quaid.
I have an appointment.

110
00:12:08,874 --> 00:12:10,291
- Bob?
- "Yeah?"

111
00:12:10,499 --> 00:12:12,665
- Doug Quaid is here to see you.
- "I'll be right out."

112
00:12:12,749 --> 00:12:14,124
OK.

113
00:12:14,332 --> 00:12:16,232
That'll be just one minute, Mr. Quaid.

114
00:12:17,499 --> 00:12:19,291
Thank you.

115
00:12:26,624 --> 00:12:29,999
- Doug! Bob McClane. Good to see you.
- Nice to meet you.

116
00:12:30,207 --> 00:12:32,666
Come on in. Through here.

117
00:12:33,499 --> 00:12:35,290
Go and have a seat.
Make yourself comfortable.

118
00:12:35,374 --> 00:12:36,582
Thank you.

119
00:12:36,791 --> 00:12:38,374
Now, help me out here, Doug.

120
00:12:38,582 --> 00:12:41,666
- You were interested in a memory of...
- Of Mars.

121
00:12:42,374 --> 00:12:43,874
Yeah. Mars.

122
00:12:44,082 --> 00:12:46,457
- Is there a problem?
- Uh...

123
00:12:47,499 --> 00:12:50,665
To be perfectly honest with you, Doug,
if outer space is your thing,

124
00:12:50,749 --> 00:12:53,624
you'd be much happier
with one of our Saturn cruises.

125
00:12:53,832 --> 00:12:55,249
Everybody raves about them.

126
00:12:55,457 --> 00:12:58,166
No. I'm not interested in Saturn.
I said Mars.

127
00:12:59,166 --> 00:13:01,249
OK. You're the boss.

128
00:13:01,999 --> 00:13:03,874
Mars it is.

129
00:13:04,666 --> 00:13:06,291
Now, let me see.

130
00:13:06,499 --> 00:13:11,791
The basic Mars package
will run you 899 credits.

131
00:13:11,999 --> 00:13:15,399
Now, that's for two full weeks
of memories, complete in every detail.

132
00:13:15,499 --> 00:13:16,540
If you want a longer trip,

133
00:13:16,624 --> 00:13:18,974
that'll cost you more
cos it's a deeper implant.

134
00:13:19,082 --> 00:13:21,374
What's in the two-week package?

135
00:13:21,582 --> 00:13:24,999
When you go Rekall, you get nothing
but first-class memories.

136
00:13:26,374 --> 00:13:30,248
Private cabin on the shuttle, deluxe suite
at the Hilton, all the major sights:

137
00:13:30,332 --> 00:13:35,124
Mount Pyramid, the Grand Canals
and of course, Venusville.

138
00:13:35,332 --> 00:13:36,999
But how real does it seem?

139
00:13:37,207 --> 00:13:41,291
- As real as any memory in your head.
- Come on. Don't bullshit me.

140
00:13:41,499 --> 00:13:44,332
No. I'm telling you, Doug.
Your brain will not know the difference.

141
00:13:44,416 --> 00:13:46,466
And that's guaranteed or your money back.

142
00:13:46,624 --> 00:13:49,832
What about the guy you lobotomized?
Did he get a refund?

143
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:55,582
You're talking ancient history.

144
00:13:55,791 --> 00:13:59,582
Nowadays, traveling with Rekall
is safer than getting on a rocket.

145
00:13:59,791 --> 00:14:01,666
Check out those statistics.

146
00:14:01,874 --> 00:14:05,374
Besides, a real holiday
is a pain in the butt.

147
00:14:05,582 --> 00:14:10,249
You got lost luggage, lousy weather,
crooked taxi drivers.

148
00:14:10,457 --> 00:14:15,666
When you travel with Rekall,
everything is perfect.

149
00:14:15,874 --> 00:14:17,957
So, what do you say?

150
00:14:19,082 --> 00:14:21,666
- All right.
- Smart move.

151
00:14:21,874 --> 00:14:25,124
All right,
while you fill out this questionnaire,

152
00:14:25,332 --> 00:14:27,832
I'm going to familiarize you
with some of our options.

153
00:14:27,916 --> 00:14:29,499
No options.

154
00:14:30,374 --> 00:14:33,749
Whatever you say.
Can I ask you just one question?

155
00:14:34,874 --> 00:14:36,749
What is that is exactly the same

156
00:14:36,957 --> 00:14:39,874
about every single vacation
you have ever taken?

157
00:14:40,957 --> 00:14:42,166
I give up.

158
00:14:42,374 --> 00:14:44,916
You. You're the same.

159
00:14:45,124 --> 00:14:48,474
No matter where you go, there you are.
It's always the same old you.

160
00:14:48,666 --> 00:14:52,541
Let me suggest that you take
a vacation from yourself.

161
00:14:52,749 --> 00:14:54,291
I know, it sounds wild.

162
00:14:54,499 --> 00:14:57,332
It is the latest thing in travel.
We call it the Ego Trip.

163
00:14:57,416 --> 00:14:59,416
No. I'm not interested in that.

164
00:14:59,624 --> 00:15:01,291
You're gonna love this, Doug.

165
00:15:01,499 --> 00:15:04,999
We offer you a choice of
alternate identities during your trip.

166
00:15:05,207 --> 00:15:08,707
Why go to Mars as a tourist,
when you can go as a playboy?

167
00:15:08,916 --> 00:15:11,832
- Or a famous jock or...?
- "Secret agent."

168
00:15:12,041 --> 00:15:13,666
How much is that?

169
00:15:15,041 --> 00:15:18,249
A-ha! Let me tantalize you.

170
00:15:19,416 --> 00:15:24,041
You are a top operative under deep cover
on your most important mission.

171
00:15:24,249 --> 00:15:26,707
People are trying to kill you.
Left and right!

172
00:15:26,916 --> 00:15:29,832
You meet this beautiful, exotic woman.

173
00:15:30,041 --> 00:15:31,124
Go on.

174
00:15:31,332 --> 00:15:33,874
I don't wanna spoil it for you, Doug,

175
00:15:34,082 --> 00:15:36,124
but by the time the trip is over,

176
00:15:36,332 --> 00:15:40,207
you get the girl, kill the bad guys
and save the entire planet.

177
00:15:40,416 --> 00:15:45,082
Now, you tell me.
Isn't that worth a measly 300 credits?

178
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:01,624
- Your first trip?
- Mm-hm.

179
00:16:01,832 --> 00:16:04,999
Well, don't worry. Things hardly ever
fuck up around here.

180
00:16:06,041 --> 00:16:07,999
Good evening... Doug.

181
00:16:08,207 --> 00:16:10,249
- I'm Dr. Lull.
- Nice to meet you.

182
00:16:10,457 --> 00:16:14,249
Ernie, patch in matrix 62-8-37.

183
00:16:14,457 --> 00:16:17,291
And would you like us
to integrate some alien stuff?

184
00:16:17,499 --> 00:16:19,582
Sure. Why not?

185
00:16:20,916 --> 00:16:24,207
- Two-headed monsters?
- Don't you keep up with the news?

186
00:16:24,416 --> 00:16:27,957
- We're doing alien artifacts now.
- It's wild.

187
00:16:28,166 --> 00:16:30,791
Yeah, they date back a million years.

188
00:16:32,166 --> 00:16:33,832
- Ernie?
- That's a new one.

189
00:16:34,041 --> 00:16:35,991
- Blue sky on Mars.
- Been married long?

190
00:16:36,832 --> 00:16:39,416
- Eight years.
- Oh, I see.

191
00:16:39,624 --> 00:16:41,791
Slipping away for a little hanky-panky.

192
00:16:41,999 --> 00:16:44,707
- No. I'm fascinated with Mars.
- All systems go.

193
00:16:44,916 --> 00:16:46,666
Then we're set.

194
00:16:46,874 --> 00:16:49,624
Ready for dreamland?

195
00:16:50,791 --> 00:16:54,832
I'll be asking you some questions
so we can fine-tune the Ego program.

196
00:16:55,041 --> 00:16:57,991
You answer honestly,
you'll enjoy yourself a whole lot more.

197
00:16:58,082 --> 00:17:00,791
- Your sexual orientation.
- Hetero.

198
00:17:06,332 --> 00:17:08,332
So, how do you like your women?

199
00:17:08,541 --> 00:17:11,291
Blonde? Brunette? Redhead?

200
00:17:12,124 --> 00:17:13,416
Brunette.

201
00:17:15,832 --> 00:17:20,166
Slim. Athletic. Voluptuous.

202
00:17:23,166 --> 00:17:24,499
Athletic.

203
00:17:28,957 --> 00:17:32,749
Demure. Aggressive. Sleazy.

204
00:17:32,957 --> 00:17:35,957
- Be honest.
- Sleazy.

205
00:17:39,957 --> 00:17:41,416
Demure.

206
00:17:44,332 --> 00:17:46,124
41A, Ernie.

207
00:17:47,541 --> 00:17:49,499
Boy, is he gonna have a wild time.

208
00:17:50,666 --> 00:17:54,041
- He's not gonna want to come back.
- Oh, that's for sure.

209
00:18:15,332 --> 00:18:16,332
So

210
00:18:16,541 --> 00:18:18,291
What do you say?

211
00:18:18,499 --> 00:18:21,374
I'm not so sure,
and I don't get a souvenir.

212
00:18:21,582 --> 00:18:23,707
Not true. For just a few more credits,

213
00:18:23,916 --> 00:18:26,666
we supply T-shirts,
snapshots of you at the site,

214
00:18:26,874 --> 00:18:28,707
and even letters from...

215
00:18:28,916 --> 00:18:32,166
"Bob!"

216
00:18:32,374 --> 00:18:34,574
- What is it?
- "You'd better get down here."

217
00:18:34,666 --> 00:18:36,666
I am with a very important client.

218
00:18:36,874 --> 00:18:39,624
"Looks like we got
another schizoid embolism."

219
00:18:41,041 --> 00:18:43,707
- I'll be right back.
- Uh... Mr. McClane?

220
00:18:43,916 --> 00:18:47,207
- Mr. McClane?
- Bob! What's wrong?

221
00:18:47,416 --> 00:18:49,332
Don't let her leave!

222
00:18:54,041 --> 00:18:55,707
Get off!

223
00:18:55,916 --> 00:18:57,499
Ah!

224
00:18:57,707 --> 00:18:59,291
You blew my cover!

225
00:18:59,499 --> 00:19:02,582
What's going on? You can't do
a simple goddamn double implant?

226
00:19:02,791 --> 00:19:04,540
It's not my fault we hit a memory cap.

227
00:19:04,624 --> 00:19:07,041
They'll be here any minute!
They'll kill you all!

228
00:19:07,249 --> 00:19:09,541
- What is he talking about?
- Let me go!

229
00:19:09,749 --> 00:19:11,499
Mr. Quaid, try to calm down!

230
00:19:13,666 --> 00:19:15,916
My name is not Quaid.

231
00:19:16,124 --> 00:19:18,874
- Let me go! Untie me now!
- Ernie, grab his leg!

232
00:19:19,082 --> 00:19:20,582
- Untie me!
- Hold him down!

233
00:19:20,791 --> 00:19:22,666
Let me go!

234
00:19:29,249 --> 00:19:30,832
Ah!

235
00:19:46,416 --> 00:19:48,332
Are you all right?

236
00:19:48,541 --> 00:19:51,791
Listen to me.
He's been going on and on about Mars.

237
00:19:51,999 --> 00:19:54,707
- He has really been there.
- Use your head, you dumb bitch.

238
00:19:54,791 --> 00:19:58,082
He's just acting out the "secret agent"
portion of his ego trip.

239
00:19:58,291 --> 00:20:00,082
- I'm afraid that's not possible.
- Why not?

240
00:20:00,166 --> 00:20:01,966
Because we haven't implanted it yet.

241
00:20:06,041 --> 00:20:07,332
Oh, shit.

242
00:20:07,541 --> 00:20:08,874
Oh, shit!

243
00:20:09,082 --> 00:20:12,416
I've been trying to tell you,
someone has erased his memory.

244
00:20:12,624 --> 00:20:15,666
Excuse me. "Someone"?

245
00:20:15,874 --> 00:20:17,874
We're talking about the fucking Agency.

246
00:20:18,082 --> 00:20:21,166
- Shut up!
- Bob, the client's gone.

247
