488
00:44:39,999 --> 00:44:42,249
Look at that shit.

489
00:44:42,457 --> 00:44:45,916
- What the hell's this?
- The Martians love Kuato.

490
00:44:46,124 --> 00:44:48,174
They think he's fuckin"
George Washington.

491
00:44:48,291 --> 00:44:49,874
Kill the bastard.

492
00:44:50,082 --> 00:44:51,582
Nobody knows who he is.

493
00:44:53,332 --> 00:44:55,541
Have you brought
any fruits or vegetables?

494
00:44:55,749 --> 00:44:57,541
Two weeks.

495
00:44:58,832 --> 00:45:00,166
Excuse me?

496
00:45:00,374 --> 00:45:02,832
Two weeks.

497
00:45:03,999 --> 00:45:06,166
Two weeks!

498
00:45:09,999 --> 00:45:14,666
It's not just graffiti. The rebels
took over the refinery last night.

499
00:45:14,874 --> 00:45:16,749
No terbinium is going out.

500
00:45:16,957 --> 00:45:18,416
And it gets worse.

501
00:45:18,624 --> 00:45:20,541
T-w-o...

502
00:45:38,999 --> 00:45:40,207
Quaid.

503
00:45:41,499 --> 00:45:43,041
- That's Quaid!
- Where?

504
00:45:43,249 --> 00:45:44,791
The woman!
Get him... her!

505
00:45:45,957 --> 00:45:47,374
Arrest that woman!

506
00:45:47,582 --> 00:45:48,916
Get that woman. Grab her!

507
00:46:18,832 --> 00:46:19,791
Catch!

508
00:46:22,166 --> 00:46:24,207
Get ready for a surprise!

509
00:47:09,916 --> 00:47:10,874
Ah!

510
00:47:34,999 --> 00:47:36,999
- Open the goddamn door!
- I can't!

511
00:47:37,207 --> 00:47:38,374
Open it!

512
00:47:38,582 --> 00:47:40,374
They're all connected!

513
00:47:49,666 --> 00:47:50,957
That's terrible.

514
00:47:51,166 --> 00:47:53,165
A few days ago
Cohaagen raised the price of air.

515
00:47:53,249 --> 00:47:54,374
Again?

516
00:47:54,582 --> 00:47:56,957
Nobody on Earth gives a damn
what happens up here.

517
00:47:57,041 --> 00:47:59,582
They just want our terbinium
so they can fight their war.

518
00:47:59,666 --> 00:48:01,541
Excuse me. What's that?

519
00:48:01,749 --> 00:48:03,749
You mean the Pyramid Mine?

520
00:48:03,957 --> 00:48:07,291
I used to work there until
they found that alien shit inside.

521
00:48:07,499 --> 00:48:09,749
Well, that's a rumor, isn't it?

522
00:48:10,082 --> 00:48:11,207
Think so?

523
00:48:40,957 --> 00:48:42,249
Mr. Cohaagen.

524
00:48:49,874 --> 00:48:51,999
You wanted to see me, sir?

525
00:48:55,374 --> 00:48:56,791
Richter...

526
00:48:58,082 --> 00:49:00,082
Do you know why I'm such a happy person?

527
00:49:00,166 --> 00:49:01,457
No, sir.

528
00:49:03,666 --> 00:49:06,874
Because I've got the greatest job
in the solar system.

529
00:49:07,082 --> 00:49:10,874
As long as the terbinium keeps flowing,
I can do anything I want.

530
00:49:11,291 --> 00:49:12,874
Anything.

531
00:49:14,249 --> 00:49:17,332
In fact, the only thing
that I ever worry about

532
00:49:17,541 --> 00:49:22,874
is that one day, if the rebels win,
it all might end,

533
00:49:24,082 --> 00:49:25,882
and you're fucking making it happen!

534
00:49:26,791 --> 00:49:29,624
First you try to kill Quaid,
then you let him get away.

535
00:49:29,832 --> 00:49:32,082
He had help from our side, sir.

536
00:49:33,166 --> 00:49:34,207
I know that.

537
00:49:36,666 --> 00:49:38,748
- But I thought...
- Who told you to think?

538
00:49:38,832 --> 00:49:41,791
I don't give you enough information
to think.

539
00:49:43,999 --> 00:49:46,999
You do what you're told.
That's what you do.

540
00:49:49,541 --> 00:49:50,957
Yes, sir.

541
00:49:51,666 --> 00:49:53,582
Now...

542
00:49:55,874 --> 00:49:57,374
Let's get to business.

543
00:49:59,249 --> 00:50:01,457
We've got a tricky situation here.

544
00:50:01,666 --> 00:50:03,874
Kuato wants what's in Quaid's head.

545
00:50:05,666 --> 00:50:08,541
And he might be able to get it,
cos they say he's psychic.

546
00:50:10,249 --> 00:50:13,291
And I have a plan
to keep this from happening.

547
00:50:16,791 --> 00:50:18,373
Do you think you could play along?

548
00:50:18,457 --> 00:50:20,457
- Yes, sir.
- Great.

549
00:50:20,666 --> 00:50:22,999
Cos otherwise, I'll erase your ass.

550
00:50:37,916 --> 00:50:41,249
You've got some
identification? Yeah, you too.

551
00:50:41,457 --> 00:50:45,332
Taxi? You need a taxi, sir?
I got magazines, music, whisky.

552
00:50:45,541 --> 00:50:48,082
Hey, man, you need a cab, man?
Come on! Come on!

553
00:51:13,124 --> 00:51:14,749
Good afternoon. Can I help you?

554
00:51:14,957 --> 00:51:17,374
Yes, I would like to have a room, please.

555
00:51:22,957 --> 00:51:25,540
Nice to have you back, Mr. Brubaker.
Would you like the same suite?

556
00:51:25,624 --> 00:51:27,332
Oh, definitely.

557
00:51:29,332 --> 00:51:31,416
Seems you've left something in our safe.

558
00:51:31,624 --> 00:51:33,624
Could you get it, please?

559
00:51:38,666 --> 00:51:40,124
Identification?

560
00:51:49,749 --> 00:51:52,582
- I'll encode your room key.
- Thank you.

561
00:52:08,457 --> 00:52:11,874
- Suite 610 in the east wing.
- Thank you.

562
00:52:12,082 --> 00:52:14,666
- Could I borrow your pen, please?
- Certainly.

563
00:52:26,416 --> 00:52:27,457
Thank you.

564
00:52:32,916 --> 00:52:35,249
Hey, man, you need a cab?

565
00:52:35,457 --> 00:52:39,791
- What's wrong with this one?
- He ain't got five kids to feed.

566
00:52:39,999 --> 00:52:43,082
- Where's yours?
- Right over there, man.

567
00:52:43,291 --> 00:52:45,332
Hey! Hey, man.

568
00:52:45,541 --> 00:52:47,291
Hey, asshole! That's my fare!

569
00:52:47,499 --> 00:52:49,916
- Eat this!
- Damn you, Benny!

570
00:52:56,541 --> 00:52:57,916
Welcome to Mars, man!

571
00:53:02,249 --> 00:53:03,873
What the hell was that, an accident?

572
00:53:03,957 --> 00:53:07,249
That's the rebels, man.
Let's get outta here...

573
00:53:07,457 --> 00:53:09,207
Before they arrest us!

574
00:53:09,416 --> 00:53:11,082
What do the rebels want?

575
00:53:11,291 --> 00:53:14,624
The usual.
More money, more freedom, more air.

576
00:53:19,832 --> 00:53:20,957
So, where to?

577
00:53:21,166 --> 00:53:22,791
Last Resort.

578
00:53:22,999 --> 00:53:24,874
You're getting off to an early start.

579
00:53:25,999 --> 00:53:28,166
- First time on Mars?
- Yes.

580
00:53:28,374 --> 00:53:31,582
Well, actually, no. Well, sort of.

581
00:53:31,791 --> 00:53:35,874
The man don't even know
whether he's been to Mars or not.

582
00:53:46,499 --> 00:53:48,832
Voila. Venusville.

583
00:53:49,041 --> 00:53:52,249
Ha, ha!
Hey, you see anything you like?

584
00:53:56,582 --> 00:53:59,632
Well, this is the end of the line.
We'd better walk from here.

585
00:53:59,832 --> 00:54:01,707
I'll show you where.

586
00:54:01,916 --> 00:54:05,416
- Do you want to know the future?
- What about the past?

587
00:54:05,624 --> 00:54:09,249
Come on. It's around the corner,
right down this alley.

588
00:54:09,457 --> 00:54:11,499
They got everything.

589
00:54:14,166 --> 00:54:15,749
Not bad, huh?

590
00:54:17,499 --> 00:54:21,832
Read your palm? Your mind? Your aura?
Probe the secrets of your heart?

591
00:54:22,041 --> 00:54:24,124
I bet I can guess your birthday.

592
00:54:24,332 --> 00:54:27,457
- You're a Taurus, right?
- How did you guess?

593
00:54:29,957 --> 00:54:32,124
- Tell me, are all psychics...?
- Freaks?

594
00:54:32,332 --> 00:54:34,373
Afraid so, man.
It goes with the territory.

595
00:54:34,457 --> 00:54:39,332
- What happened to them?
- Cheap domes, no air to clean the rays.

596
00:54:39,541 --> 00:54:43,374
So, this is it. The Last Resort.
You sure you want to go in here?

597
00:54:43,582 --> 00:54:46,916
- Why not?
- There's a better place down there.

598
00:54:47,124 --> 00:54:49,824
The girls are cleaner,
the liquor ain't watered down...

599
00:54:49,957 --> 00:54:52,249
Sure, and you get kickbacks.

600
00:54:52,457 --> 00:54:55,249
Hey, man, I got five kids to feed.

601
00:54:55,457 --> 00:54:56,916
Take them to the dentist.

602
00:54:57,124 --> 00:54:59,624
Hey, thanks, mister!
I'll be waiting for you.

603
00:54:59,832 --> 00:55:01,916
You just take your time.
Benny's the name.

604
00:55:22,207 --> 00:55:24,248
- What do you want?
- I'm looking for Melina.

605
00:55:24,332 --> 00:55:25,999
She's busy.

606
00:55:26,207 --> 00:55:27,874
But Mary here, she's free.

607
00:55:28,791 --> 00:55:31,374
Well, not free, honey, but

608
00:55:32,291 --> 00:55:33,707
available.

609
00:55:34,541 --> 00:55:36,374
Ha-ha-ha!

610
00:55:36,582 --> 00:55:38,832
Thanks. I'll wait for Melina.

611
00:55:39,041 --> 00:55:40,124
Earth slime.

612
00:55:40,332 --> 00:55:42,874
Thing is, friend, Mel's real picky.

613
00:55:43,082 --> 00:55:45,291
She kind of sticks to her regulars.

614
00:55:45,499 --> 00:55:46,957
She'll like me.

615
00:55:48,499 --> 00:55:49,666
Mel!

616
00:55:49,874 --> 00:55:51,374
Hey, Mel!

617
00:56:27,416 --> 00:56:28,999
Hello, Hauser.

618
00:56:29,999 --> 00:56:31,624
Still bulging, I see.

619
00:56:33,207 --> 00:56:36,332
- What you been feeding this thing?
- Blondes.

620
00:56:38,291 --> 00:56:40,457
I think it's still hungry.

621
00:56:42,791 --> 00:56:45,748
You got a lot of nerve
showing your face around here, Hauser.

622
00:56:45,832 --> 00:56:47,707
Look who's talking.

623
00:56:47,916 --> 00:56:50,624
Hey, Tony, give the big guy a break.

624
00:56:50,832 --> 00:56:53,041
Relax. You'll live longer.

625
00:56:53,249 --> 00:56:54,999
Come on.

626
00:57:00,291 --> 00:57:03,457
- Honey, take care of Tony, will you?
- No problem.

627
00:57:03,957 --> 00:57:07,082
If you need any help with this one,
give me a holler.

628
00:57:21,957 --> 00:57:23,749
You son of a bitch.

629
00:57:23,957 --> 00:57:26,665
You're alive? I thought that
Cohaagen tortured you to death.

630
00:57:26,749 --> 00:57:28,499
Well, I guess he didn't.

631
00:57:28,707 --> 00:57:32,416
And you couldn't get me a message?
You never wondered what happened to me?

632
00:57:40,082 --> 00:57:42,291
Hauser, thank God you're alive.

633
00:57:43,499 --> 00:57:45,749
Melin... Melina. Melina.

634
00:57:46,749 --> 00:57:50,624
- Melina, I have to tell you something.
- What?

635
00:57:50,832 --> 00:57:54,291
- I don't remember you.
- What are you talking about?

636
00:57:54,499 --> 00:57:56,582
I don't remember you.

637
00:57:56,791 --> 00:58:00,041
I don't remember us.
I don't even remember me.

638
00:58:02,291 --> 00:58:04,541
Did you get amnesia?
How did you get here?

639
00:58:04,749 --> 00:58:07,123
- Hauser left me a note.
- Hauser? You're Hauser.

640
00:58:07,207 --> 00:58:09,041
Not anymore.

641
00:58:09,249 --> 00:58:12,207
Now I'm Quaid. Douglas Quaid.

642
00:58:15,499 --> 00:58:19,457
- Hauser, you've lost your mind.
- I didn't. Cohaagen stole it.

643
00:58:19,666 --> 00:58:24,082
He found out that Hauser switched sides,
so he turned him into somebody else: Me.

644
00:58:24,291 --> 00:58:25,624
This is too weird.

645
00:58:25,832 --> 00:58:28,332
He dumped me on earth
with a wife and a lousy job...

646
00:58:28,416 --> 00:58:31,207
Did you say wife?
Are you fucking married?

647
00:58:31,416 --> 00:58:33,457
- She wasn't really my wife.
- Oh, she isn't?

648
00:58:33,541 --> 00:58:35,749
How stupid of me.
She was Hauser's wife?

649
00:58:35,957 --> 00:58:39,040
- Look. Forget that I said wife.
- Let's just forget everything.

650
00:58:39,124 --> 00:58:42,666
- I'm sick of hearing your goddamn lies.
- Why would I lie to you?

651
00:58:43,791 --> 00:58:47,041
Because you're still
working for Cohaagen.

652
00:58:47,249 --> 00:58:49,166
Don't be ridiculous.

653
00:58:52,541 --> 00:58:54,541
You never loved me, Hauser.

654
00:58:54,749 --> 00:58:56,624
You just used me to get inside.

655
00:58:56,832 --> 00:58:58,791
Inside what?

656
00:59:02,874 --> 00:59:04,832
I think you'd better leave.

657
00:59:05,041 --> 00:59:08,082
- Hauser sent me to do something.
- I'm not falling for it.

658
00:59:08,291 --> 00:59:10,540
He says there's enough in here
to nail Cohaagen for good.

659
00:59:10,624 --> 00:59:12,540
- Get out!
- You've got to help me remember!

660
00:59:12,624 --> 00:59:14,707
- I said, get out!
- Melina, please!

661
00:59:14,916 --> 00:59:16,582
People are trying to kill me.

662
00:59:17,582 --> 00:59:18,666
Really?

663
00:59:21,582 --> 00:59:23,541
All right, I'm leaving.

664
00:59:35,416 --> 00:59:38,457
Baby, you make me wish I had three hands.

665
00:59:38,666 --> 00:59:41,249
I think you're doing just fine with two.

666
00:59:41,457 --> 00:59:43,707
Excuse me, baby.
We'll pick this up later.

667
00:59:43,916 --> 00:59:46,207
Hey, that didn't take long.

668
00:59:46,416 --> 00:59:48,998
Listen. Let me ask you a question.
Did you ever fuck a mutant?

669
00:59:49,082 --> 00:59:51,540
- Take me to the hotel.
- I know these Siamese twins.

670
00:59:51,624 --> 00:59:54,666
Man, you won't know
if you're coming or going.

671
01:00:03,999 --> 01:00:07,624
"This afternoon at 4:30pm,
I signed an order declaring martial law"

672
01:00:07,832 --> 01:00:09,874
"throughout the Mars federal colony."

673
01:00:10,082 --> 01:00:14,791
"I will not tolerate any further damage
to our mineral export operations."

674
01:00:14,999 --> 01:00:17,082
"Mr. Kuato and his terrorists
must understand"

675
01:00:17,166 --> 01:00:20,866
"that their self-defeating efforts
will only bring misery and suffering..."

676
01:00:24,416 --> 01:00:27,207
- Mr. Quaid?
- What?

677
01:00:27,416 --> 01:00:30,207
I need to talk to you about Mr. Hauser.

678
01:00:31,124 --> 01:00:33,291
- Who are you?
- Dr. Edgemar from Rekall.

679
01:00:33,499 --> 01:00:35,748
- How did you find me?
- It's difficult to explain.

680
01:00:35,832 --> 01:00:38,916
Could you open the door?
I'm unarmed.

681
01:00:40,957 --> 01:00:43,291
Don't worry. I'm alone.
May I come in?

682
01:00:45,207 --> 01:00:46,374
What do you want?

683
01:00:46,582 --> 01:00:48,915
This is going to be very difficult
for you to accept, Mr. Quaid.

684
01:00:48,999 --> 01:00:53,916
- I'm listening.
- You're not really standing here now.

685
01:00:54,124 --> 01:00:57,082
- Doc, you could have fooled me.
- I'm quite serious.

686
01:00:57,291 --> 01:01:00,332
You're not here and neither am I.

687
01:01:00,541 --> 01:01:01,832
That's amazing.

688
01:01:02,041 --> 01:01:04,666
- Where are we?
- At Rekall.

689
01:01:05,291 --> 01:01:06,957
You're strapped into an implant chair,

690
01:01:07,041 --> 01:01:10,291
and I'm monitoring you
from the psychoprobe console.

691
01:01:11,291 --> 01:01:13,666
Ah, I get it. I'm dreaming.

692
01:01:13,874 --> 01:01:17,165
And all this is part of the delightful
vacation your company has sold me.

693
01:01:17,249 --> 01:01:18,541
Not exactly.

694
01:01:18,749 --> 01:01:22,791
What you're experiencing is a free-form
delusion based on our memory tapes

695
01:01:22,999 --> 01:01:25,957
but you're inventing it yourself
as you go along.

696
01:01:27,082 --> 01:01:30,416
If it is my delusion,
who the hell invited you?

697
01:01:30,624 --> 01:01:34,249
I've been artificially implanted
as an emergency measure.

698
01:01:34,457 --> 01:01:37,807
I'm sorry to tell you this,
but you've suffered a schizoid embolism.

699
01:01:37,916 --> 01:01:40,082
We can't snap you out of your fantasy,

700
01:01:40,291 --> 01:01:43,374
and I've been sent in
to try to talk you down.

701
01:01:43,582 --> 01:01:45,632
How much is Cohaagen paying you for this?

702
01:01:46,832 --> 01:01:50,916
Think about it. Your dream started
in the middle of the implant procedure.

703
01:01:51,124 --> 01:01:53,457
Everything after that,
the chases, the trip to Mars,

704
01:01:53,541 --> 01:01:57,916
the suite at the Hilton, are elements
of your Rekall Holiday and Ego Trip.

705
01:01:58,124 --> 01:02:00,374
You paid to be a secret agent.

706
01:02:00,582 --> 01:02:02,957
Bullshit. It's coincidence.

707
01:02:03,791 --> 01:02:05,791
And what about the girl?

708
01:02:05,999 --> 01:02:08,499
Brunette, athletic, sleazy and demure?

709
01:02:08,707 --> 01:02:11,041
Just as you specified.
Is that coincidence?

710
01:02:11,249 --> 01:02:14,749
She's real. I dreamt about her
before I even went to Rekall.

711
01:02:14,957 --> 01:02:16,916
Ha, Mr. Quaid.

712
01:02:17,124 --> 01:02:21,041
Can you hear yourself?
She's real because you dreamed her?

713
01:02:21,249 --> 01:02:24,124
- That's right.
- Maybe this will convince you.

714
01:02:24,999 --> 01:02:27,207
Would you mind opening the door?

715
01:02:28,707 --> 01:02:33,166
- You open it.
- No need to be rude. I'll do it.

716
01:02:39,582 --> 01:02:40,749
Sweetheart?

717
01:02:43,416 --> 01:02:45,791
Come in, Mrs. Quaid.

718
01:02:49,666 --> 01:02:54,291
- I suppose you're not here either.
- I'm here... at Rekall.

719
01:02:58,999 --> 01:03:00,666
I love you.

720
01:03:00,874 --> 01:03:04,082
Right.
That's Why you tried to kill me.

721
01:03:04,291 --> 01:03:07,332
No. I'd never do anything
to hurt you.

722
01:03:08,332 --> 01:03:10,791
I want you to come back to me.

723
01:03:12,874 --> 01:03:15,999
- Bullshit.
- What's bullshit, Mr. Quaid?

724
01:03:16,207 --> 01:03:18,057
That you're having a paranoid episode

725
01:03:18,207 --> 01:03:20,749
triggered by acute neurochemical trauma?

726
01:03:20,957 --> 01:03:24,791
Or that you're really an invincible
secret agent from Mars,

727
01:03:24,999 --> 01:03:28,999
who's the victim of an interplanetary
conspiracy to make him think

728
01:03:29,207 --> 01:03:31,041
he's a lowly construction worker?

729
01:03:38,707 --> 01:03:40,916
Stop punishing yourself, Doug.

730
01:03:41,124 --> 01:03:44,624
You're a fine, upstanding man.
You have a beautiful wife who loves you.

731
01:03:45,582 --> 01:03:47,632
- Your whole life is ahead of you.
- I do.

732
01:03:49,541 --> 01:03:52,082
But you've got to want
to return to reality.

733
01:03:54,499 --> 01:03:57,082
Let's assume I do. Then what?

734
01:03:59,999 --> 01:04:02,999
- Swallow this.
- What is it?

735
01:04:03,207 --> 01:04:06,416
It's a symbol of your desire
to return to reality.

736
01:04:07,332 --> 01:04:09,916
Inside your dream, you'll fall asleep.

737
01:04:13,541 --> 01:04:18,166
All right, let's say you're telling
the truth and this is all a dream.

738
01:04:18,374 --> 01:04:20,415
Then I could pull this trigger
and it won't matter.

739
01:04:20,499 --> 01:04:23,416
- Doug, don't.
- It won't make a difference to me.

740
01:04:23,624 --> 01:04:27,999
But the consequences to you would be
devastating. In your mind I'll be dead.

741
01:04:28,207 --> 01:04:31,582
With no one to guide you out,
you'll be stuck in permanent psychosis.

742
01:04:31,666 --> 01:04:33,832
Doug, let Dr. Edgemar help you.

743
01:04:34,041 --> 01:04:36,207
The walls of reality
will come crashing down.

744
01:04:36,291 --> 01:04:38,540
One minute you'll be
the savior of the rebel cause,

745
01:04:38,624 --> 01:04:42,041
and the next thing you know
you'll be Cohaagen's bosom buddy.

746
01:04:42,249 --> 01:04:46,124
You'll even have fantasies about
alien civilizations, as you requested,

747
01:04:46,332 --> 01:04:48,882
but in the end, back on earth
you'll be lobotomized!

748
01:04:51,499 --> 01:04:55,416
So get a grip on yourself, Doug,
and put down that gun!

749
01:05:01,082 --> 01:05:04,749
Good. Now take the pill
and put it in your mouth.

750
01:05:09,332 --> 01:05:10,999
Swallow it!

751
01:05:14,249 --> 01:05:15,999
Go ahead, sweetheart.

752
01:05:38,791 --> 01:05:41,957
Now you've done it.
Now you've done it!

753
01:05:56,749 --> 01:05:58,082
Ah!

754
01:06:01,957 --> 01:06:02,790
Aargh!

755
01:06:02,916 --> 01:06:05,291
That's for making me come to Mars.

756
01:06:06,707 --> 01:06:10,082
You know how much I hate
this fucking planet!

757
01:06:11,916 --> 01:06:13,166
Cuff him.

758
01:06:19,916 --> 01:06:23,291
- "I got him."
- Bring him down in the service elevator.

759
01:06:25,457 --> 01:06:26,999
Let's go.

760
01:07:40,332 --> 01:07:41,374
Fuck you!

761
01:07:51,999 --> 01:07:53,166
Doug.

762
01:07:55,207 --> 01:07:57,207
Honey...

763
01:07:57,416 --> 01:07:59,832
You wouldn't hurt me,
would you, sweetheart?

764
01:08:01,707 --> 01:08:04,874
Sweetheart, be reasonable.

765
01:08:05,082 --> 01:08:07,207
After all, we're married.

766
01:08:12,624 --> 01:08:14,041
Consider that a divorce.

767
01:08:16,624 --> 01:08:18,207
That was your wife?

768
01:08:22,291 --> 01:08:23,541
What a bitch.

769
01:08:31,791 --> 01:08:33,916
Hey, get out of the way!

770
01:08:37,249 --> 01:08:38,874
I thought you didn't like me.

771
01:08:39,082 --> 01:08:41,666
If Cohaagen wants you dead,
you might be OK.

772
01:08:41,874 --> 01:08:45,207
- Got it.
- So you've come back to apologize.

773
01:08:45,416 --> 01:08:47,041
Kuato wants to see you.

774
01:08:49,166 --> 01:08:50,707
Come on.

775
01:09:19,041 --> 01:09:20,499
- Now what?
- Jump!

776
01:09:24,416 --> 01:09:26,082
Ah!

777
01:09:50,249 --> 01:09:53,999
No! Don't do it!
You'll crack the fucking dome!

778
01:09:57,582 --> 01:10:00,832
What are you trying to do, kill us?
The dome will crack!

779
01:10:13,207 --> 01:10:14,624
- Move!
- Hey!

780
01:10:16,207 --> 01:10:18,082
Taxi!

781
01:10:18,957 --> 01:10:21,082
Melina! Melina!

782
01:10:24,207 --> 01:10:25,707
- Need a ride?
- Last Resort. Quick!

783
01:10:25,791 --> 01:10:27,291
You guys are going in circles.

784
01:10:32,291 --> 01:10:33,166
Jesus!

785
01:10:33,374 --> 01:10:35,457
Come on! You drive!

786
01:10:35,666 --> 01:10:36,790
You guys are in trouble?

787
01:10:36,874 --> 01:10:38,582
Go! Go!

788
01:10:49,374 --> 01:10:52,166
- What are you trying to do to me?
- Shut up and drive!

789
01:10:52,374 --> 01:10:54,499
Hey, I got five kids to feed!

790
01:11:10,582 --> 01:11:12,291
Aargh!

791
01:11:28,582 --> 01:11:29,666
Shit!

792
01:11:29,874 --> 01:11:31,541
- No brakes! Ah!
- Stop it!

793
01:11:31,749 --> 01:11:33,249
You idiot!

794
01:11:36,582 --> 01:11:37,532
What are you doing?

795
01:11:50,374 --> 01:11:53,082
Oh, Christ! Now they're after me!

796
01:11:54,374 --> 01:11:55,541
Give me that!

797
01:11:55,749 --> 01:11:57,707
Get out of the way!

798
01:11:59,832 --> 01:12:01,291
Hey!

799
01:12:04,207 --> 01:12:05,582
Tony!

800
01:12:09,291 --> 01:12:11,666
Get out of the way!
Come on!

801
01:12:11,874 --> 01:12:14,207
Come on! Come on!

802
01:12:14,416 --> 01:12:15,624
Quick!

803
01:12:17,666 --> 01:12:18,966
- Thank you, Tony.
- Uh-um.

804
01:12:42,291 --> 01:12:46,041
Hey! You wanna have some fun?

805
01:12:46,249 --> 01:12:47,332
Where are they?

806
01:12:47,541 --> 01:12:50,207
What are you talking about?
I don't know.

807
01:12:58,457 --> 01:12:59,957
Maybe you know.

808
01:13:07,249 --> 01:13:08,499
Kill them all!

809
01:13:19,957 --> 01:13:21,332
Ah!

810
01:13:22,749 --> 01:13:24,207
Thumbelina!

811
01:13:48,999 --> 01:13:50,416
Richter!

812
01:13:50,624 --> 01:13:53,874
- A call from Cohaagen!
- Richter here.

813
01:13:54,082 --> 01:13:56,873
- We've got them pinned down.
- "Stop fighting and pull out."

814
01:13:56,957 --> 01:13:59,207
But they've got Quaid.
They're protecting him.

815
01:14:00,082 --> 01:14:03,166
"Perfect.
Get out of Sector G now."

816
01:14:03,374 --> 01:14:04,791
"Don't think."

817
01:14:04,999 --> 01:14:07,332
- "Do it!"
- Yes, sir.

818
01:14:07,541 --> 01:14:09,332
Pull 'em out.

819
01:14:09,541 --> 01:14:11,791
Everybody, pull out!

820
01:14:11,999 --> 01:14:13,541
Move!

821
01:14:22,374 --> 01:14:25,499
- Cohaagen's sealing off the area!
- Come on, Benny!

822
01:15:27,207 --> 01:15:28,957
The first settlers are buried here.

823
01:15:29,124 --> 01:15:33,041
They worked themselves to death, but
Cohaagen ended up with all the money.

824
01:15:33,249 --> 01:15:35,915
He built cheap domes and
watched the kids turn into freaks.

825
01:15:35,999 --> 01:15:37,124
I saw them.

826
01:15:37,332 --> 01:15:39,916
And if you want to breathe,
you have to buy his air.

827
01:15:40,124 --> 01:15:41,624
Maybe you can change all that.

828
01:15:42,499 --> 01:15:45,916
Hey, I think my grandpa might be here.

829
01:15:46,124 --> 01:15:47,666
So what can I do?

830
01:15:47,874 --> 01:15:50,623
Kuato's gonna make you remember some
things you knew when you were Hauser.

831
01:15:50,707 --> 01:15:53,166
- Like what?
- All sorts of things.

832
01:15:53,374 --> 01:15:56,724
- Maybe you'll remember you loved me.
- I don't need Kuato for that.

833
01:15:57,624 --> 01:15:59,457
Since when?

834
01:16:09,291 --> 01:16:10,916
Freeze!

835
01:16:11,124 --> 01:16:12,791
Come on, Melina.

836
01:16:14,082 --> 01:16:15,332
Kuato's waiting.

837
01:16:15,541 --> 01:16:18,249
I didn't find Grandpa, but...

838
01:16:18,999 --> 01:16:20,416
Oh, shit.

839
01:16:20,624 --> 01:16:23,666
- Who's this?
- He helped us get away.

840
01:16:23,874 --> 01:16:27,957
Hey, don't worry about me, man.
I'm on your side.

841
01:16:38,582 --> 01:16:40,457
You're a mutant, huh?

842
01:16:40,666 --> 01:16:42,916
All right, let's go.

843
01:16:58,124 --> 01:17:00,915
- Have you tried ramming down the door?
- You wait here. Follow me.

844
01:17:00,999 --> 01:17:02,666
"It won't do any good.

845
01:17:02,874 --> 01:17:06,248
- "Cohaagen depressurized the tunnels."
- Then drill through to Section M.

846
01:17:06,332 --> 01:17:09,207
"We can't.
We're running out of air."

847
01:17:09,416 --> 01:17:11,332
"We need help."

848
01:17:11,541 --> 01:17:14,082
Sit tight.
Melina just got here with Quaid.

849
01:17:15,207 --> 01:17:16,874
"I hope he was worth it."

850
01:17:17,082 --> 01:17:18,624
So do I.

851
01:17:21,082 --> 01:17:23,040
- I'm glad you made it.
- You don't look glad.

852
01:17:23,124 --> 01:17:26,291
Cohaagen sealed up Venusville.
He shut off the air.

853
01:17:26,499 --> 01:17:28,665
You must know something
pretty important, Quaid.

854
01:17:28,749 --> 01:17:30,707
He wants you.

855
01:17:30,916 --> 01:17:34,332
If we don't hand you over, everybody
in this sector will be dead by morning.

856
01:17:34,416 --> 01:17:36,266
Then we don't have much choice.
Do we?

857
01:17:36,416 --> 01:17:37,874
We can't turn him in.

858
01:17:39,249 --> 01:17:41,541
That's up to Kuato.
Come with me, Quaid.

859
01:17:55,707 --> 01:17:57,166
Sit down.

860
01:17:57,916 --> 01:18:00,541
- Where's Kuato?
- On his way.

861
01:18:00,874 --> 01:18:03,207
You heard the rumors
about the Pyramid Mine?

862
01:18:03,416 --> 01:18:05,166
Yeah.

863
01:18:05,374 --> 01:18:08,707
Cohaagen found something weird inside
and it's got him scared shitless.

864
01:18:08,791 --> 01:18:11,041
What? Aliens?

865
01:18:12,666 --> 01:18:15,332
- You tell me.
- I don't know.

866
01:18:15,541 --> 01:18:17,957
Yes, you do.
That's why we brought you here.

867
01:18:18,166 --> 01:18:20,666
Cohaagen's big secret
is buried in that black hole

868
01:18:20,874 --> 01:18:22,916
you call a brain.

869
01:18:25,541 --> 01:18:27,291
And Kuato's gonna dig it out.

870
01:18:27,499 --> 01:18:30,249
- You're Kuato, right?
- Wrong.

871
01:18:31,041 --> 01:18:34,916
Kuato's a mutant,
so don't get upset when you see him.

872
01:18:39,541 --> 01:18:41,374
Ah!

873
01:19:13,457 --> 01:19:15,499
What do you want, Mr. Quaid?

874
01:19:16,624 --> 01:19:18,291
The same as you. To remember.

875
01:19:18,499 --> 01:19:20,666
But why?

876
01:19:21,291 --> 01:19:24,457
- To be myself again.
- You are what you do.

877
01:19:27,957 --> 01:19:31,124
A man is defined by his actions

878
01:19:31,332 --> 01:19:33,457
not his memory.

879
01:19:34,624 --> 01:19:37,666
Please take my hands.

880
01:19:39,916 --> 01:19:41,749
Ah!

881
01:19:43,416 --> 01:19:45,874
Now open your mind to me.

882
01:19:46,999 --> 01:19:48,291
Please.

883
01:19:51,207 --> 01:19:53,916
Open your mind.

884
01:19:55,957 --> 01:19:58,416
Open your mind.

885
01:20:00,666 --> 01:20:04,332
Open your mind.

886
01:20:05,791 --> 01:20:09,416
Open your mind.

887
01:20:11,291 --> 01:20:14,916
Open your mind.

888
01:20:45,999 --> 01:20:48,799
We should blow the thing up
before the rebels turn it on.

889
01:20:48,957 --> 01:20:51,257
I say we throw the switch
and see what happens.

890
01:20:51,416 --> 01:20:53,366
- Don't be an idiot.
- We can't risk it.

891
01:20:53,541 --> 01:20:56,457
The chain reaction could spread
to all the terbinium in the planet.

892
01:20:56,541 --> 01:20:59,332
That means a meltdown,
a meltdown on a planetary scale.

893
01:20:59,541 --> 01:21:01,957
Don't you think whoever
built this thing thought of that?

894
01:21:02,041 --> 01:21:04,999
Who knows what the hell they thought?
They weren't human.

895
01:21:05,207 --> 01:21:07,624
Maybe it's a trap.
Maybe they want a meltdown.

896
01:21:07,832 --> 01:21:09,998
We don't even know
if this piece of junk will work.

897
01:21:10,082 --> 01:21:12,541
What is it?
A million? Half a million?

898
01:21:12,749 --> 01:21:15,666
- About half a million.
- Half a million years old.

899
01:21:15,874 --> 01:21:17,749
Let's make sure Kuato...

900
01:21:48,666 --> 01:21:51,999
Wake up! Wake up!
Come on, wake up!

901
01:21:53,416 --> 01:21:55,916
They found us! Shit! Let's go!

902
01:21:57,207 --> 01:21:59,832
Wake up! Snap out of it now!
Come on!

903
01:22:04,082 --> 01:22:06,916
- They found us! Everybody out!
- Melina!

904
01:22:07,124 --> 01:22:09,124
Get moving! Get out!

905
01:22:10,457 --> 01:22:12,082
Get out!

906
01:22:21,124 --> 01:22:23,166
Everybody out! Get out!

907
01:22:28,874 --> 01:22:31,207
Get to the air lock! Follow me!

908
01:22:32,957 --> 01:22:34,457
Benny, come on!

909
01:22:38,541 --> 01:22:41,124
- Benny!
- I'm coming!

910
01:22:53,332 --> 01:22:54,749
- Ah!
- This way!

911
01:23:00,374 --> 01:23:03,999
Put these spacesuits on!
We're going outside!

912
01:23:06,666 --> 01:23:08,666
Benny, hurry.

913
01:23:16,291 --> 01:23:20,291
Congratulations, Quaid.
You led us right to him.

914
01:23:20,499 --> 01:23:23,124
How can you do this?
You're a mutant.

915
01:23:24,499 --> 01:23:25,999
I got four kids to feed.

916
01:23:26,207 --> 01:23:28,249
So what happened to number five?

917
01:23:30,166 --> 01:23:33,332
Oh, shit, man. You got me.

918
01:23:33,541 --> 01:23:35,082
I ain't even married.

919
01:23:35,291 --> 01:23:37,332
Now put your fucking hands in the air!

920
01:23:43,207 --> 01:23:45,207
Quaid.

921
01:23:46,791 --> 01:23:48,791
Quaid.

922
01:23:50,374 --> 01:23:53,957
Forget it, man.
His fortunetelling days are over.

923
01:23:56,666 --> 01:23:59,374
Start the reactor.

924
01:23:59,582 --> 01:24:01,249
Free Mars.

925
01:24:06,541 --> 01:24:09,082
Mr. Cohaagen would like to talk to you.

926
01:24:17,124 --> 01:24:19,916
So this is the great man.

927
01:24:24,457 --> 01:24:26,291
No wonder he kept out of sight.

928
01:24:28,541 --> 01:24:30,291
Well, my boy...

929
01:24:33,041 --> 01:24:34,957
- You're a hero.
- Fuck you.

930
01:24:35,166 --> 01:24:38,749
Uh? Don't be modest.
Kuato is dead.

931
01:24:38,957 --> 01:24:43,166
The resistance is completely wiped out,
and you were the key to the whole thing.

932
01:24:43,374 --> 01:24:44,624
He's lying.

933
01:24:45,666 --> 01:24:48,332
You two-faced bastard.

934
01:24:49,332 --> 01:24:53,249
Ha, ha. You can't blame him, angel.
He's innocent.

935
01:24:55,041 --> 01:24:58,874
You see, Quaid, none of my people
could get close to Kuato.

936
01:24:59,457 --> 01:25:02,166
Fucking mutants
could always sniff us out.

937
01:25:02,374 --> 01:25:06,457
So Hauser and I sat down
and invented you, the perfect mole.

938
01:25:06,666 --> 01:25:09,707
You know you're lying.
Hauser turned against you.

939
01:25:13,791 --> 01:25:15,541
That's what we wanted you to think.

940
01:25:16,457 --> 01:25:19,666
The fact is, Hauser volunteered
to become Doug Quaid.

941
01:25:20,916 --> 01:25:22,832
It was the only way to fool the psychics.

942
01:25:22,916 --> 01:25:24,332
Get your story straight.

943
01:25:24,541 --> 01:25:28,040
This idiot here has been trying to kill me
ever since I went to Rekall.

944
01:25:28,124 --> 01:25:30,415
You don't kill somebody
you're trying to plant.

945
01:25:30,499 --> 01:25:34,249
He wasn't in on it.
You set him off by going to Rekall.

946
01:25:34,499 --> 01:25:37,291
- So why am I still alive?
- We gave you lots of help.

947
01:25:37,499 --> 01:25:39,249
- Benny here.
- My pleasure, man.

948
01:25:39,457 --> 01:25:42,916
The guy with the suitcase,
the mask, the money,

949
01:25:43,124 --> 01:25:46,916
the message from Hauser,
all of that was set up by us.

950
01:25:47,124 --> 01:25:49,499
Sorry. Too perfect.

951
01:25:49,707 --> 01:25:51,249
Perfect, my ass!

952
01:25:51,457 --> 01:25:53,999
You pop your memory cap
before we can activate you.

953
01:25:54,207 --> 01:25:58,124
Richter goes hog-wild, screwing up
everything I spent a year planning.

954
01:25:58,332 --> 01:26:02,041
Frankly, I'm amazed it worked.

955
01:26:02,249 --> 01:26:03,582
Well, Cohaagen,

956
01:26:03,791 --> 01:26:07,332
I have to hand it to you.
It's the best mind-fuck yet.

957
01:26:08,624 --> 01:26:11,291
Well, don't take my word for it.

958
01:26:13,124 --> 01:26:18,124
- Someone you trust wants to talk to you.
- Who is it this time? My mother?

959
01:26:20,332 --> 01:26:21,582
"Howdy, Quaid.

960
01:26:21,791 --> 01:26:25,166
"If you're listening to this,
it means that Kuato is dead

961
01:26:25,374 --> 01:26:27,624
"and you have led us to him."

962
01:26:27,832 --> 01:26:29,749
"I knew you wouldn't let me down."

963
01:26:29,957 --> 01:26:34,541
"Sorry for the shit I've put you through,
but hey, what are friends for?"

964
01:26:34,749 --> 01:26:37,916
"I would like to wish you
happiness and long life, old buddy,"

965
01:26:38,124 --> 01:26:40,916
"but unfortunately,
this is not gonna happen."

966
01:26:41,124 --> 01:26:45,166
"You see, it's my body
you've got there and I want it back."

967
01:26:45,374 --> 01:26:49,499
"Sorry to be an Indian giver,
but I was here first."

968
01:26:49,707 --> 01:26:52,249
"So adios, amigo."

969
01:26:52,457 --> 01:26:55,541
"And thanks for not
getting yourself killed."

970
01:26:55,749 --> 01:26:58,332
"Hey, maybe we'll meet in our dreams."

971
01:27:01,957 --> 01:27:03,957
"You never know."

972
01:27:08,624 --> 01:27:10,749
You bastards'!

973
01:27:28,791 --> 01:27:30,124
Let go of me!

974
01:27:46,457 --> 01:27:48,332
- Ready?
- Auto.

975
01:27:48,541 --> 01:27:51,541
- Check.
- Ready to go, sir.

976
01:27:53,541 --> 01:27:55,624
Relax, Quaid.

977
01:27:55,832 --> 01:27:59,124
- You'll like being Hauser.
- The guy's a fucking asshole.

978
01:27:59,332 --> 01:28:02,416
Not true.
He's one of my best friends.

979
01:28:02,624 --> 01:28:05,416
Besides, he's got
a big house and a Mercedes.

980
01:28:05,624 --> 01:28:09,541
And you like Melina, right?
You'll get to fuck her every night.

981
01:28:09,749 --> 01:28:12,582
That's right.
She's going to be Hauser's babe.

982
01:28:12,791 --> 01:28:14,874
I'll bust his balls.

983
01:28:17,249 --> 01:28:19,249
Uh-uh, princess.

984
01:28:19,457 --> 01:28:21,916
We're having you fixed.

985
01:28:22,124 --> 01:28:25,249
You're going to be respectful, compliant

986
01:28:25,457 --> 01:28:28,791
and appreciative,
the way a woman should be.

987
01:28:32,749 --> 01:28:34,832
Mr. Cohaagen, telephone.

988
01:28:37,499 --> 01:28:39,124
Yes? What is it?

989
01:28:39,332 --> 01:28:41,916
"The oxygen level
is bottoming out in Sector G."

990
01:28:42,124 --> 01:28:44,249
"What do you want me
to do about it?"

991
01:28:44,457 --> 01:28:48,416
- Don't do anything.
- "But they won't last an hour, sir."

992
01:28:48,624 --> 01:28:50,957
Fuck 'em. It'll be a good lesson
to the others.

993
01:28:51,166 --> 01:28:54,874
Come on, you got what you want.
Give these people air.

994
01:28:55,082 --> 01:28:58,832
My friend, in five minutes
you won't give a shit about the people.

995
01:28:59,041 --> 01:29:00,041
Fire it up, Doc.

996
01:29:00,249 --> 01:29:02,249
Excuse me, Doctor.

997
01:29:02,457 --> 01:29:04,907
- Is he gonna remember any of this?
- Not a thing.

998
01:29:05,624 --> 01:29:06,666
Oh, really?

999
01:29:17,249 --> 01:29:20,624
Quaid, I'm having a party tonight.
Why don't you and Melina drop by?

1000
01:29:20,832 --> 01:29:22,291
- Remind him, Doc.
- Sure.

1001
01:29:22,499 --> 01:29:23,999
See you at the party.

1002
01:29:38,749 --> 01:29:41,041
Keep still.
Fighting just makes it hurt.

1003
01:29:53,916 --> 01:29:56,624
If you don't keep still,
you'll end up psychotic.

1004
01:30:01,041 --> 01:30:02,249
Hey, don't!

1005
01:30:09,332 --> 01:30:10,916
Melina, hold on!

1006
01:30:33,916 --> 01:30:37,249
Are you all right?
Are you still you?

1007
01:30:37,457 --> 01:30:40,832
I'm not sure, dear.
What do you think?

1008
01:30:43,749 --> 01:30:46,291
Let's get the hell out of here.

1009
01:31:12,374 --> 01:31:14,624
You have to make a decision, sir.

1010
01:31:25,207 --> 01:31:26,374
Kill him.

1011
01:31:27,707 --> 01:31:29,707
It's about goddamn time.

1012
01:32:21,999 --> 01:32:24,582
- Where are you going?
- To the reactor.

1013
01:32:24,791 --> 01:32:28,374
- What reactor?
- The one in the mines. Come on!

1014
01:32:28,582 --> 01:32:32,499
People are dying, Quaid!
Stop! We've got to get air!

1015
01:32:32,707 --> 01:32:35,791
The reactor makes air.
That's Cohaagen's secret. Let's go.

1016
01:32:35,999 --> 01:32:37,498
Where's this reactor come from?

1017
01:32:37,582 --> 01:32:39,499
- Aliens built it.
- Aliens?

1018
01:32:39,707 --> 01:32:43,082
- Are you sure about this?
- It's just up ahead.

1019
01:32:45,707 --> 01:32:47,916
What the hell?

1020
01:33:11,374 --> 01:33:15,332
Quaid! Hey, Quaid,
you remember me?

1021
01:33:15,541 --> 01:33:17,749
Benny! Benny's the name!

1022
01:33:31,999 --> 01:33:33,374
Oh, that's good!

1023
01:33:39,249 --> 01:33:43,457
I'm gonna drill you, sucker!
I'm gonna grind you up!

1024
01:33:49,249 --> 01:33:52,499
Ha-ha! I'm coming!

1025
01:33:52,707 --> 01:33:54,249
I'm coming for you, baby!

1026
01:34:09,999 --> 01:34:11,957
What the fuck is this?

1027
01:34:18,624 --> 01:34:20,624
Damn this piece of Martian junk!

1028
01:34:22,999 --> 01:34:25,416
Hey, Quaid, I'm gonna squash you!

1029
01:34:26,791 --> 01:34:28,624
Benny, here!

1030
01:34:31,874 --> 01:34:33,416
Where the fuck are you?

1031
01:34:39,207 --> 01:34:40,832
Screw you!

1032
01:34:46,999 --> 01:34:50,832
- Quaid, get over here!
- What is it?

1033
01:34:51,874 --> 01:34:55,666
- There's an opening.
- I knew it.

1034
01:35:24,499 --> 01:35:27,666
This whole thing is one big reactor
made out of terbinium.

1035
01:35:27,874 --> 01:35:31,082
Cohaagen knows it makes air.
The bastard won't turn it on.

1036
01:35:31,291 --> 01:35:35,916
Of course not. If Mars had
an atmosphere, he'd lose control.

1037
01:35:36,791 --> 01:35:38,041
See down there?

1038
01:35:39,291 --> 01:35:41,582
It's a glacier.

1039
01:35:41,791 --> 01:35:44,791
The whole core of Mars is ice.

1040
01:35:44,999 --> 01:35:49,166
The reactor melts it
and it releases the oxygen.

1041
01:35:49,374 --> 01:35:50,582
Come on.

1042
01:35:50,791 --> 01:35:53,666
- Enough for everyone to breathe?
- Sure.

1043
01:35:53,874 --> 01:35:56,666
Enough for the whole planet.

1044
01:35:56,874 --> 01:35:59,166
If we turn it on in time.

1045
01:36:05,791 --> 01:36:07,791
Come on. Come on!

1046
01:36:24,707 --> 01:36:25,832
Hold on.

1047
01:36:57,291 --> 01:36:58,707
Now!

1048
01:37:28,541 --> 01:37:29,707
Son of a bitch.

1049
01:37:37,541 --> 01:37:39,207
Move!

1050
01:37:41,957 --> 01:37:43,999
He's got a hologram!

1051
01:38:05,957 --> 01:38:08,499
You think this is
the real Quaid? It is.

1052
01:39:28,207 --> 01:39:30,416
You're coming with me!

1053
01:39:44,166 --> 01:39:46,374
See you at the party, Richter.

1054
01:40:24,666 --> 01:40:29,082
- Don't touch that! Get back!
- What are you afraid of?

1055
01:40:29,291 --> 01:40:31,541
- Turn it on.
- Impossible!

1056
01:40:31,749 --> 01:40:34,915
Once the reaction starts, it'll spread
to all the terbinium in the planet.

1057
01:40:34,999 --> 01:40:37,166
Mars will go into global meltdown.

1058
01:40:37,374 --> 01:40:39,874
That's why the aliens never turned it on.

1059
01:40:40,082 --> 01:40:42,041
And you expect me to believe you?

1060
01:40:42,249 --> 01:40:46,791
Who gives a shit what you believe?
In 30 seconds you'll be dead.

1061
01:40:46,999 --> 01:40:50,166
Then I'll blow this place up
and be home in time for cornflakes.

1062
01:40:53,916 --> 01:40:57,791
I didn't want it to end this way.
I wanted Hauser back. But no.

1063
01:40:59,207 --> 01:41:01,166
You had to be Quaid!

1064
01:41:01,374 --> 01:41:03,707
- I am Quaid.
- You're nothing!

1065
01:41:03,916 --> 01:41:06,916
You're nobody!
You're a stupid dream.

1066
01:41:07,124 --> 01:41:10,999
Well, all dreams come to an end.

1067
01:42:25,832 --> 01:42:28,041
Melina, hold on!

1068
01:42:28,249 --> 01:42:31,791
Don't do it! We'll all die!

1069
01:42:32,791 --> 01:42:35,124
Everybody will die!

1070
01:43:38,249 --> 01:43:39,666
Quaid!

1071
01:48:54,541 --> 01:48:57,207
I can't believe it.
It's like a dream.

1072
01:48:58,249 --> 01:48:59,707
What's wrong?

1073
01:48:59,916 --> 01:49:03,749
I just had a terrible thought.
What if this is a dream?

1074
01:49:05,249 --> 01:49:08,749
Well, then kiss me quick
before you wake up.

